Title:
Kestrel — Native Active Directory “what’s already inside” auditor (persistence, misconfig, posture)

Type:
GitHub Tool

Short Summary (4-8 sentences max):
Kestrel is a single, native Windows executable that performs read-only Active Directory and SYSVOL auditing to find high-impact security issues that typical graph/path tools (e.g., BloodHound) don’t model well. It focuses on “directory-resident” backdoors and misconfigurations such as attribute-based persistence (shadow credentials, SIDHistory), schema defaultSecurityDescriptor backdoors, hidden objects via deny-read ACEs, and tombstone reanimation rights. It also audits AD CS/AD FS prerequisites (ESC1–5/9, NTAuth store, AD FS DKM key ACLs), delegation configurations (unconstrained/constrained/RBCD/S4U), credential exposure in SYSVOL (GPP cpassword, unattend/sysprep/script creds), and posture gaps (policies, LAPS coverage, stale systems). The tool runs as an ordinary domain user, avoids replication APIs (detects DCSync rights without performing DCSync), and documents its on-DC footprint event-by-event in FOOTPRINT.md. Output includes prioritized findings with remediation hints, HTML/JSON/YAML reports, diffs against prior snapshots, and optional export to BloodHound CE OpenGraph. It’s useful for red/purple teams for fast, low-friction AD auditing and for blue teams to baseline, detect drift, and remediate Tier-0 exposures.

Technical Focus:
- Active Directory ACL/ACE analysis (DCSync rights, deny-read “hidden” objects, inheritance/owner hygiene)
- Attribute-based persistence (msDS-KeyCredentialLink shadow creds, sIDHistory, adminCount/AdminSDHolder)
- AD CS/PKI abuse auditing (ESC1–5/9, NTAuth store, template/CA misconfig)
- AD FS DKM key permissions (Golden SAML precondition)
- Delegation abuse (unconstrained, constrained, RBCD, S4U2Self)
- SYSVOL secret discovery + credential attack surface (GPP cpassword, Kerberoast/AS-REP roast, LAPS gaps)

Use Cases:
- Baseline an AD environment for Tier-0 persistence and misconfigurations missed by path-only analysis
- Identify principals with DCSync capability without triggering replication-specific telemetry
- Audit AD CS templates/CAs and NTAuth for common escalation paths (ESC series)
- Check AD FS DKM ACL exposure to assess Golden SAML risk
- Hunt for stealthy directory objects (deny-read) and schema-level backdoors
- Generate weekly diffs to detect newly introduced risky permissions/persistence

Keywords:
Active Directory, LDAP, SYSVOL, Windows, ACL, ACE, DCSync rights, GetChanges, GetChangesAll, delegation, unconstrained delegation, constrained delegation, RBCD, S4U2Self, AD CS, ESC1, ESC2, ESC3, ESC4, ESC5, ESC9, NTAuth store, AD FS, DKM key, Golden SAML, msDS-KeyCredentialLink, shadow credentials, sIDHistory, AdminSDHolder, adminCount, GPP cpassword, Kerberoasting, AS-REP roasting, LAPS, BloodHound CE, OpenGraph, replication metadata